  "notes": [
    "C-stick directions reach original forward/up/down smash states 60/63/64 without synthesizing A presses.",
    "Analog shoulders retain magnitude and remain distinct from digital L/R bits; original fighter code applies deadzones and combines shoulder pressure.",
    "Keyboard grab now passes native Z directly. Main-stick keyboard diagonals stay inside the unit circle, with Alt providing half magnitude.",
    "Standard gamepad layout follows the existing browser button layout. Browser pressed flags do not turn halfway analog travel into a hard shield; digital clicks are mapped at 99% travel.",
    "Unit coverage includes both slots, held-input clearing on blur/disconnection/stop and rejection of malformed samples.",
    "No physical controller was connected or latency measured. Device calibration, nonstandard GameCube adapters and native pause/menu lifecycle remain unfinished.",
    "Timing runs use hardware-rendered headless Chrome and the deterministic combat workload, excluding startup/intro. Counted draw submissions are not proof of distinct screen presentations.",
    "Fountain uses the existing cosmetic reductions with original moving platforms and camera; all four Ice Climbers remain active."
  ],
